From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:11:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: <|assistant|> ends a reply,
 TF_GLM_ASSISTANT_ENDS (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0075)

At high reasoning effort GLM-5.3 sometimes wrote its <|assistant|> role token inside its answer and began a second
one, and the raw token reached the reply's text, which agents then fed back into the conversation (the recipe's
issue #60, reported by Lukas-tek-no-logic). MiaAI-Lab's recipe v1.6 ends the reply there, like the checkpoint's end
tokens (<|endoftext|>, <|user|>, <|observation|>), with patch 0075-glm-assistant-ends: the token's id is read from the
checkpoint's tokenizer.json and joins Config.eos, which every decode loop, the multi-stream decoder, the grammar and
the server's text use on every rank, and the startup comparison checks the ranks agree. This ports it with the
recipe's own switch, TF_GLM_ASSISTANT_ENDS, but off by default here (the recipe's default is 1):

- weights.py: assistant_end, verbatim but for the default (unset or 0: None; 1: the token's id; anything else is
  refused); Config.read adds the token to eos when it is on, verbatim.
- engine.py: the end tokens' count and sum in the ranks' startup row and TF_GLM_ASSISTANT_ENDS in its refusal, as in
  the patch (the row has them whatever the switch; with it off they are the checkpoint's own, so both ranks agree as
  before), on a line of their own after the KV kind's, so that line reads as before (tests/test_glm_kv8.py checks its
  source); a startup line when the token ends replies.
- tests/test_cuda_capacity.py: its fake GLM Config has end tokens, as Config does (the startup row now reads them).
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md: "GLM assistant ends".

Unset, Config.eos is the checkpoint's end tokens, as before.

Tests: tests/test_glm_assistant_ends.py (8, CPU): the switch's values (unset, empty and 0 off; 1 on; others refused);
only the special <|assistant|> of a readable tokenizer.json is added, once; GlmEngine's start up to the ranks'
comparison with no device or weights: the row differs only in the end tokens' count and sum, and a rank on with one
off refuses to start, naming the switch; a reply through the single-stream engine and two ranks' multi-stream
decoders over the fake model, with one of its tokens standing for <|assistant|>: off it runs past the token, on it
ends there, and a second stream decoding beside it is unchanged.

Credit: patch 0075 was written by MiaAI-Lab (https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab) for
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold issue #60, reported by Lukas-tek-no-logic
(https://github.com/Lukas-tek-no-logic), in recipe commit 5859365 (v1.6), Apache License 2.0.

Changed from the picked commit: the end tokens join the startup row with a line of their own (mine += [...]) instead
of inside the KV kind's line; the row is the same, in the same order.

